# React

Always write functional components instead of class components.

Access elements of the `React` namespace, rather than importing them individually. (eg. `React.useState`, `React.Fragment`).

Use the `React.FC<{}>` type when defining React components.

Make use of the `react-use` utility hook library as needed.

Prefer writing `<React.Fragment>` over the shorthand `</>`, for better readability.

Only use memoization techniques when there is a clear issue being to resolve. Don't pre-optimize.
